+(in <code class="code">&lt;threads.h&gt;</code>);
+<code class="code">mbstate_t</code> (in <code class="code">&lt;wchar.h&gt;</code>).
+</p></blockquote>
+
+<p>In theory, portable code should not use <code class="code">malloc</code> to
+allocate storage containing types not in this list;
+it should instead use functions like <code class="code">aligned_alloc</code>.
+In practice, though, other implementations generally follow
+the GNU C Library&rsquo;s lead and define only types with fundamental alignment,
+and it is generally portable to use <code class="code">malloc</code> to allocate objects
+with types defined by the C library.
+</p></li></ul>
 
